ngement visually demonstrates how a sub-array is a contiguous section of a =
larger array, selected by its starting and ending indices.  The indices are=
 used to access specific elements within the array." loading=3D"lazy" width=
=3D"225" height=3D"38" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" style=3D"color:tr=
ansparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/courses/coding-patterns/pre=
fix-sums/sum-between-range/image-10-01-3-H55BHFLR.svg?dpl=3Ddpl_CEjisbLnWxF=
QGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure>
<p>Is there a way to get this using only prefix sums? All prefix sum values=
 are sums for ranges that start at index 0. So, let=E2=80=99s see how we co=
uld make use of these ranges. Consider the sum of the range [0, 4], which c=
orresponds to <code>prefix_sum[4]</code>:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
