 6, 0, -2], with indices [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] shown faintly below each element. =
 Above this array, a bright-blue line segment extends horizontally, marked =
with small perpendicular lines at its ends. A small triangle points downwar=
ds from the line segment, positioned above the element '0' at index 3.  The=
 text 'sum[0 : 4]' is written in blue above the line, indicating that a sum=
 is being calculated from index 0 up to (but not including) index 4.  The n=
umber '5' is shown outside the light-blue rectangle to the right, likely re=
presenting an element beyond the sub-array being considered. The overall im=
age illustrates a sub-array selection and a potential summation operation w=
ithin a larger array context." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"235" height=3D"61"=
